; worldquest.eval — a quest moves, and a clue puts a place on the map (P6).
;
; The design's own two sentences, made testable:
;   "you might find a quest item in a dungeon. This will update some quest flags
;    for the overall world."
;   "you might find a map or a clue that will add them."
;
; STAGES ARE NAMED, NOT NUMBERED, and the save carries the name — so this checks
; the NAME comes back, which an index could not distinguish from a reordering.
logecho on
reset
encounters off

; --- nothing found yet -------------------------------------------------------
quest
world

; --- the clue: moves the quest to `heard` AND reveals the back way -----------
give crypt_token
quest
world

; --- the relic: moves it to `found`, and sets a plain flag too ---------------
give sunken_relic
quest
quest flags

; --- and all of it rides the save -------------------------------------------
save questtrip
load questtrip
quest
quest flags
world
